  "$schema-note": "Literal upstream iconify names -> b24-icons components. READ FIRST: b24ui shares nuxt/ui's SEMANTIC icon keys (src/runtime/dictionary/icons.ts vs upstream src/theme/icons.ts), so when a diff references `appConfig.ui.icons.<key>` or `icons.<key>`, KEEP the key unchanged — b24ui already resolves it to the right b24-icon. This table is only for the cases where upstream HARDCODES a literal `i-lucide-*` string. Most entries are derived, not chosen: for every key both sides define, the pair is (upstream's lucide name -> b24ui's component). The exceptions, which are judgement calls rather than derivations: `i-lucide-circle-check` is upstream's `success`, a key b24ui does not have (mapped to the same glyph as `copyCheck`, so two upstream names share one component here on purpose); `i-lucide-refresh-cw` is b24ui's `refresh`, a key upstream does not have; and activity/arrow-up-to-line/house/settings/user predate the derivation and match no key on either side. Upstream keys with no b24ui counterpart (error, eye, eyeOff, folder, folderOpen, success) have no entry — pick a component during the port and add it here in the same commit (PORTING.md §4).",
